'''''Polygala fruticosa''''', the '''sweet pea shrub''', is a species of flowering plant in the milkwort family ([[Polygalaceae]]). It is native to Eswatini and Kwazulu-Natal and the Cape Provinces in South Africa.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Polygala fruticosa P.J.Bergius {{!}} Plants of the World Online {{!}} Kew Science|url=https://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:691467-1|access-date=2020-06-08|website=Plants of the World Online}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Polygala fruticosa {{!}} International Plant Names Index|url=https://www.ipni.org/n/691467-1|access-date=2020-06-08|website=www.ipni.org}}</ref> It was first [[species description|described]] by [[Peter Jonas Bergius]] in&nbsp;1767.<ref name="ipni">{{cite web |author1=Harvard University |author2=Royal Botanic Gardens Kew |author3=Australian National Herbarium |title=Polygala fruticosa |url=https://www.ipni.org/n/691467-1 |website=International Plant Names Index |accessdate=July 24, 2020}}</ref> According to the Red List of South African Plants, it is of least ecological concern.<ref name="redlist">{{cite web |author1=South African National Biodiversity Institute |title=Polygala fruticosa P.J.Bergius |url=https://redlist.sanbi.org/species.php?species=3614-32 |website=Red List of South African Plants |accessdate=July 24, 2020}}</ref>

